<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul bourse says computer systems normalised.</title>
<headline>Seoul bourse says computer systems normalised.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Korea Stock Exchange's computer systems were back to normal at 3.40 p.m. (0640 GMT) after crashing for 48 minutes, an exchange spokesman said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The spokesman said after-hour trading, originally scheduled from 3.10-3.40 p.m. (0610-0640 GMT), was delayed by 40 minutes.</p>
<p>He did not elaborate on the cause of the malfunction.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
